;; Australia (national) national holidays 2000-2040: external gold for AU.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_americas_holiday_gold.py AU
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "AU"
 :generated "2026-11-27"
 :from 2000 :to 2040
 :note "National subset: the Fair Work Act s. 115 holidays that every State and Territory keeps on the same day, with the substitute days every jurisdiction gives. The King's (Queen's) Birthday is left out (WA and QLD keep it on other days), as are Easter Saturday and Sunday, Labour Day, Melbourne Cup and other state days. A weekend holiday stays a holiday on its own day; the substitute day is added. The state acts differ on whether a weekend Australia Day or New Year's Day itself stays a holiday, and the official data set lists them inconsistently, so its weekend days are not compared."
 :sources
 (
  (:title "Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth) s. 115" :uri "https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2009A00028/latest/text"
   :text "Public holidays: 1 January, 26 January, Good Friday, Easter Monday, 25 April, the King's birthday holiday (on the day each State or Territory celebrates it), 25 and 26 December, and a day a State or Territory law substitutes for one of them (s. 115(2)-(3)).")
  (:title "State and territory public holiday acts" :uri "https://www.fairwork.gov.au/employment-conditions/public-holidays"
   :text "Every State and Territory adds the Monday after a Saturday or Sunday New Year's Day or Australia Day, and moves Christmas Day and Boxing Day off a weekend to the next free weekdays. Anzac Day has no substitute in every jurisdiction, so none here.")
  (:title "Australian Public Holidays Dates Machine Readable Dataset (PM&C, data.gov.au)" :uri "https://data.gov.au/data/dataset/australian-holidays-machine-readable-dataset"
   :text "Official per-jurisdiction lists 2014-2025. The national subset (days listed for all of ACT, NSW, NT, QLD, SA, TAS, VIC, WA) agrees with this fixture on every weekday except 2022-09-22, which the 2022 file (March 2022) predates.")
  (:title "National Day of Mourning for Queen Elizabeth II, 22 September 2022" :uri "https://www.fairwork.gov.au/newsroom/news/national-day-of-mourning-public-holiday"
   :text "A one-off public holiday declared in every State and Territory.")
 )
